        <mxCell id="title" value="Prometheus 3.14.0: one server process, from service discovery to a fired alert" style="text;html=1;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Times New Roman;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="960" height="26" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="cap" value="Figure 1. What one Prometheus server does between two scrapes. (1) discovery.Manager polls the configured SD sources and re-emits the whole&lt;br&gt;target set. (2) scrape.Manager keeps one scrapePool per job and lets relabel_configs rewrite the discovered labels into one URL per target.&lt;br&gt;(3) One scrapeLoop per target issues the HTTP GET and parses the reply. (4) storage.Fanout hands every sample to the local TSDB first.&lt;br&gt;(5) The TSDB logs to wal/ before memory, cuts the Head into a 2 h block, and merges blocks upward. (6) rules.Manager evaluates the rule&lt;br&gt;files and appends its results back into the same database. (7) promql.Engine reads the Head and the blocks together. (8) notifier.Manager&lt;br&gt;batches firing alerts out. Every arrow that crosses the green boundary is started from inside it, and nothing outside it holds state that this&lt;br&gt;server needs to answer a query. Source: local checkout of the repository, VERSION 3.14.0, commit not determined (the folder has no .git)." style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#4a4a4a;fontFamily=Times New Roman;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1000" width="960" height="124" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

